# ---- 767 Public Management ----
H("767.c.5",3,"A course syllabus lists skills students should master, such as budgeting, writing reports and communicating with the public. These are the knowledge and skills for the course of study in:","public management",["pottery making","stage lighting","farm equipment repair"],"Courses state knowledge and skills to master.")
H("767.c.5",4,"In a public management class, the 'knowledge and skills' section of the standards tells students:","what they are expected to learn and be able to do",["what the lunch menu is","who the school mascot is","when the bell rings"],"Standards list expected learning.")
H("767.d.1.A",3,"A student charts how a city's public works department answers to voters and elected boards, while a food bank answers to donors and its own board. This compares and contrasts management of:","government and nonprofit agencies",["two sports teams","two restaurants","two movie studios"],"Accountability differs.")
H("767.d.1.A",4,"A key difference between a government agency and a nonprofit is that a government agency is funded mainly by:","taxes and appropriations",["ticket sales","product sales","investor dividends"],"Government relies on public funding.")
H("767.d.1.B",3,"A department posts a mission to protect clean drinking water, then sets goals that support the larger agency's vision. A student compares:","department vision, goals and mission to support the agency's",["colors of department logos","office furniture","lunch schedules"],"Department goals support agency mission.")
H("767.d.1.B",4,"A department's goals should align with:","the larger organization's vision and mission",["unrelated hobbies","random ideas","a competitor's plan"],"Alignment keeps efforts coordinated.")
H("767.d.2.A",3,"A new parks manager joins a professional association, meets county staff and partners with a school district. This develops:","expansive professional networks internally and with other organizations",["isolated work habits","private hobbies","closed circles"],"Networks aid cooperation.")
H("767.d.2.A",4,"A benefit of a strong professional network for a public manager is:","easier sharing of ideas and resources",["less information","more isolation","fewer contacts"],"Networks share resources.")
H("767.d.2.B",3,"A hiring team practices posting jobs in many places and interviewing a wide range of candidates to build a staff reflecting the community. This practices the process of:","recruiting a diverse workforce",["avoiding applicants","hiring only friends","closing positions"],"Diverse recruitment widens the pool.")
H("767.d.2.B",4,"To recruit a diverse applicant pool, an agency should:","advertise openings widely and in varied outlets",["post only internally","rely on word of mouth","hide the opening"],"Broad outreach.")
H("767.d.2.C",3,"When two departments clash over shared space, a manager listens, finds common ground and turns the dispute into a joint plan. This applies:","interpersonal skills to manage conflicts positively",["avoidance to end talks","blaming to win","silence to wait"],"Interpersonal skills resolve conflict.")
H("767.d.2.C",4,"A productive way to handle a workplace conflict is to:","listen to both sides and seek common ground",["ignore it","take a side at once","complain to others"],"Active listening.")
H("767.d.2.D",3,"A director opens each staff meeting by connecting daily tasks to the agency's vision, mission and goals. This emphasizes the need to:","infuse understanding of vision, mission and goals into all work",["hide the mission","separate staff from goals","skip planning"],"Mission shapes daily work.")
H("767.d.2.D",4,"Reminding employees how their tasks support the agency's mission can:","increase focus and motivation",["reduce clarity","lower morale","confuse priorities"],"Purpose motivates.")
H("767.d.2.E",3,"A county compares the chance of a flood against the cost of buying insurance and building barriers, then picks a plan. This analyzes the concept of:","risk management",["risk avoidance only","risk creation","risk denial"],"Risk management weighs likelihood and cost.")
H("767.d.2.E",4,"Risk management includes:","identifying, assessing and reducing risks",["ignoring risks","creating risks","hiding risks"],"The standard steps.")
H("767.d.2.F",3,"Before voting on the annual budget, a city gives notice of the meeting so residents may attend. This legally publicizes:","meetings at which budget and allocation decisions will be made",["private parties","secret deals","closed sessions"],"Open meeting laws require notice.")
H("767.d.2.F",4,"Public notice of a budget meeting helps ensure that decisions are:","made openly with citizen input",["made in secret","made without input","made by one person"],"Transparency.")
H("767.d.3.A",3,"A supervisor finds staff reluctant to share drafts and templates, fearing others will take credit. She sets credit rules and sharing norms. This addresses:","reluctance of employees to share work product and intellectual property",["lack of lunch breaks","parking complaints","dress codes"],"Clear credit norms encourage sharing.")
H("767.d.3.A",4,"A manager can encourage sharing of work product by:","recognizing and crediting contributors",["hiding credit","punishing sharing","banning teamwork"],"Credit builds trust.")
H("767.d.3.B",3,"A water engineer explains a new treatment rule to residents using everyday words and a simple chart. This restates complex technical information in:","language the general public can understand",["language only engineers know","legal jargon","code words"],"Plain language aids understanding.")
H("767.d.3.B",4,"The best way to explain a technical issue to the public is to:","use plain language and clear examples",["use jargon","use long reports","use acronyms only"],"Use plain language.")
H("767.d.3.C",3,"A city manager explains why the council raised a fee, gives the reasons and answers residents' questions at a forum. This explains, justifies and discusses:","public issues effectively",["private jokes","sports trades","recipes"],"Explain and justify decisions.")
H("767.d.3.C",4,"When justifying a public decision, a manager should give:","clear reasons and supporting facts",["only slogans","no reasons","personal insults"],"Reasons build trust.")
H("767.d.3.D",3,"A spokesperson practices staying calm, answering truthfully and redirecting when a reporter asks a hostile question. This presents techniques to handle:","difficult interviews and situations",["easy tasks only","quiet days","routine filing"],"Prepare for tough questions.")
H("767.d.3.D",4,"If asked a hostile question in an interview, the best response is to:","stay calm and answer factually",["lose your temper","refuse to talk","change the subject rudely"],"Calm and factual.")
H("767.d.3.E",3,"A clerk follows the same rules whether a reporter or a resident asks to see a public record. This affords the public:","equal opportunity of access to open records",["secret access","preferred access","no access"],"Open records are equally available.")
H("767.d.3.E",4,"Under open-records laws, most government records are:","available to any member of the public on request",["private forever","for officials only","sold to bidders"],"Public access.")
H("767.d.4.A",3,"An analyst pulls budget numbers, staffing counts and service results from a city and from a comparable nonprofit to compare them. This obtains:","relevant data on public and non-public management",["recipes","travel photos","sports scores"],"Gather relevant data.")
H("767.d.4.A",4,"Relevant data for comparing two agencies could include:","budgets, staffing and service outcomes",["favorite colors","pet names","weather"],"Comparable metrics.")
H("767.d.4.B",3,"A researcher uses surveys, cost-benefit analysis and trend charts to study a new program. This applies:","pertinent research and analytical methodologies",["random guessing","hearsay","wishful thinking"],"Use sound methods.")
H("767.d.4.B",4,"A cost-benefit analysis compares a project's:","expected costs and expected benefits",["colors and fonts","names and dates","songs and videos"],"Costs versus benefits.")
H("767.d.4.C",3,"Before closing a bus route, a manager studies how many riders it will affect and for what trips. This assesses:","the impact of probable changes on the public",["last year's menu","a sports score","a parade route"],"Predict public impact.")
H("767.d.4.C",4,"Before a policy change, managers should consider how it will affect:","the people who use the service",["only the managers","only the budget","no one"],"Impact on users.")
H("767.d.5.A",3,"A budget analyst prices a new library branch using government accounting standards and consistent categories. This estimates costs according to:","standards for government accounting",["personal opinion","guesswork","rumor"],"Use standard accounting.")
H("767.d.5.A",4,"Following accounting standards when estimating costs ensures:","consistent and comparable figures",["secret numbers","random numbers","inflated numbers"],"Standards ensure comparability.")
H("767.d.5.B",3,"A manager presents a low-cost, a mid-cost and a full-service version of a recreation program for the council to choose from. This proposes:","options over a range of cost requirements",["only one plan","no plan","an unlimited plan"],"Options across cost levels.")
H("767.d.5.B",4,"Giving decision-makers several cost options helps them:","choose what fits the available funds",["avoid deciding","ignore the cost","spend without limits"],"Options fit budgets.")
H("767.d.5.C",3,"A grants officer scans state and federal programs for money that could pay for new buses. This analyzes government resources to find:","possibilities for new or increased funding",["ways to cut all spending","reasons to delay","rules to avoid"],"Search for grants.")
H("767.d.5.C",4,"A government grant is money that is generally:","awarded for a specific purpose",["unrestricted gifts","personal bonuses","loans with interest"],"Grants are purpose-specific.")
H("767.d.5.D",3,"A student lists expected revenues, then allocates amounts to salaries, supplies and equipment for the department. This prepares:","a budget",["a menu","a schedule","a playlist"],"Budgets plan revenues and expenses.")
H("767.d.5.D",4,"A balanced department budget should ensure that:","planned spending does not exceed expected revenue",["spending is unlimited","revenue is unknown","costs are ignored"],"Balance revenue and spending.")
H("767.d.6.A",3,"A purchasing clerk helps program staff complete the forms, quotes and approvals needed to buy new computers under agency rules. This demonstrates how to assist staff to:","fulfill procurement requirements",["avoid purchases","skip approvals","hide costs"],"Support staff through procurement.")
H("767.d.6.A",4,"Procurement rules exist so that public money is spent:","fairly and with accountability",["secretly","freely","carelessly"],"Fair and accountable.")
H("767.d.6.B",3,"After a vendor misses deliveries, a manager suggests a change to vendor scoring and deadlines. This recommends process changes to improve:","vendor reliability and performance",["staff parking","lunch menus","office music"],"Improve vendor performance.")
H("767.d.6.B",4,"One way to improve vendor reliability is to:","set clear performance standards and review them",["ignore late work","stop paying","avoid contracts"],"Performance standards.")
H("767.d.6.C",3,"To attract many qualified bidders for a road project, the agency posts the notice online, in the paper and with trade groups. This determines:","public announcements to elicit vendor interest and bids",["secret invitations","private messages","closed offers"],"Wide notice yields competitive bids.")
H("767.d.6.C",4,"Advertising a bid widely tends to:","increase competition and lower prices",["reduce competition","raise prices","hide the project"],"Competition helps taxpayers.")
H("767.d.6.D",3,"A buyer checks that each possible supplier is licensed, insured and in good standing. This identifies:","sources that match approved vendor criteria",["random sellers","unlicensed sellers","friends only"],"Vendors must meet criteria.")
H("767.d.6.D",4,"An approved vendor list helps an agency by:","ensuring suppliers meet minimum standards",["avoiding standards","raising costs","skipping checks"],"Vetting vendors.")
H("767.d.6.E",3,"A review team scores every proposal with the same checklist and weighting so no bidder gets a break. This manages an evaluation process that ensures each bid is:","evaluated fairly and on equal terms",["favored","ignored","delayed"],"Consistent criteria.")
H("767.d.6.E",4,"Using a written scoring rubric for bids helps ensure:","fairness and consistency",["bias","secrecy","favoritism"],"Rubrics standardize.")
H("767.d.6.F",3,"An agency stores bids securely and shares a bidder's trade secrets with no competitor while also following open-bid rules. This identifies ways to safeguard:","proprietary information of bidders and the rights of the agency",["public gossip","random files","open diaries"],"Protect confidential info.")
H("767.d.6.F",4,"A bidder's pricing formula is sensitive because it is:","proprietary information",["public information","a weather report","a sports statistic"],"Proprietary data stays protected.")
H("767.d.7.A",3,"A records officer studies retention schedules and the Public Information Act so that she knows what must be released and what must be kept. This maintains thorough familiarity with:","public information requirements and records management",["recipe collections","movie reviews","fashion tips"],"Know the law and procedures.")
H("767.d.7.A",4,"A records retention schedule tells an agency:","how long to keep different records",["which songs to play","where to hold parties","what to eat"],"Retention schedules.")
H("767.d.7.B",3,"A staff member calmly explains the law and reason behind a decision to keep an investigation file confidential when someone asks for it. This identifies how to explain:","policy background and rationale to persons denied access",["a secret","an insult","a joke"],"Explain rationale respectfully.")
H("767.d.7.B",4,"When denying a records request, the agency should:","explain the legal reason and the appeal options",["ignore the request","refuse silently","shame the requester"],"Explain and inform.")
H("767.d.7.C",3,"An IT lead compares passwords, locked cabinets and access logs as ways to keep unauthorized people out of sensitive files. This compares:","reliable controls to prevent unauthorized access to records",["ways to speed access for all","ways to share passwords","ways to delete logs"],"Access controls protect records.")
H("767.d.7.C",4,"Which control best prevents unauthorized access to digital records?","unique passwords with access logs",["shared passwords","no logins","open files"],"Authentication and logging.")

# ---- 768 Regulatory / Compliance (investigation, inspection) ----
H("768.d.1.A",3,"In a mock case, a trainee follows up tips, interviews a mock client and checks where leads go to find who might have broken a rule. This investigates potential violators by:","exploring leads and conducting mock client interviews",["avoiding clues","guessing","closing the case"],"Investigators follow leads.")
H("768.d.1.A",4,"A lead is best described as:","a piece of information that may help solve a case",["a final verdict","a legal penalty","a policy statement"],"Leads guide investigation.")
H("768.d.1.B",3,"A trainee practices explaining why a witness should cooperate and how a subpoena legally requires records or testimony. This models:","persuasive and ethical techniques, such as subpoenas, to gain cooperation",["threats to force silence","bribes for answers","tricks to mislead"],"Ethical persuasion and legal tools.")
H("768.d.1.B",4,"A subpoena is a legal order that requires someone to:","provide testimony or documents",["leave town","pay a bonus","stop working"],"Subpoenas compel.")
H("768.d.1.C",3,"An investigator sorts a pile of papers into those that show the alleged violation and those that are unrelated, setting aside the second group. This identifies and differentiates:","relevant and irrelevant evidence and information",["old and new songs","red and blue pens","big and small boxes"],"Relevance matters.")
H("768.d.1.C",4,"Evidence is relevant when it:","helps prove or disprove a fact in the case",["fills a folder","is old","is interesting but unrelated"],"Relevance test.")
H("768.d.1.D",3,"A trainee photographs a document, logs who handled it and stores it sealed so it can be used at a hearing. This examines evidence while:","preserving it and observing the rules of evidence",["altering it","losing it","sharing it freely"],"Chain of custody.")
H("768.d.1.D",4,"A chain-of-custody log records:","who handled evidence and when",["the weather","the lunch order","the case outcome"],"Tracks handling.")
H("768.d.1.E",3,"A trainee reviews invoices, payroll and inspection records of a business to see whether the numbers match and the files are complete. This examines:","business, commercial, industrial and agency records for accuracy and completeness",["fashion catalogs","comic books","sports magazines"],"Record review.")
H("768.d.1.E",4,"A mismatch between invoices and payments might signal:","possible errors or fraud",["perfect accuracy","good weather","normal sunshine"],"Discrepancies deserve review.")
H("768.d.1.F",3,"In a short case report, a trainee lists what happened in order, avoids opinions and keeps sentences tight. This organizes facts:","accurately, objectively, logically and concisely",["loosely","emotionally","randomly"],"Good reports are factual.")
H("768.d.1.F",4,"A factual investigative report should avoid:","unsupported opinions",["dates","names","observations"],"Stay objective.")
H("768.d.1.G",3,"A trainee learns that peeking into someone's private home or medical file without authority is illegal. This analyzes matters that are prohibited or concern:","invasion of privacy",["public parades","open meetings","sports rules"],"Privacy limits investigators.")
H("768.d.1.G",4,"An investigator needs a legal basis, such as a warrant, before:","searching private property",["reading a public sign","walking in a park","asking a question"],"Warrants protect privacy.")
H("768.d.1.H",3,"During a role-play, a trainee watches a mock subject from a distance and notes times, places and actions without interfering. This simulates conducting:","surveillance while recording facts",["a parade","a lesson","a trade fair"],"Surveillance records observations.")
H("768.d.1.H",4,"Notes taken during surveillance should include:","dates, times, locations and observed actions",["guesses","gossip","jokes"],"Factual notes.")
H("768.d.2.A",3,"An analyst sees that a project's actual spending is far above its standard cost and investigates why. This analyzes:","the common accounting problem of costs deviating from standards",["a color mismatch","a font mismatch","a sports mismatch"],"Variance analysis.")
H("768.d.2.A",4,"When actual costs exceed the standard, the difference is called a:","variance",["bonus","quota","tariff"],"Cost variance.")
H("768.d.2.B",3,"A regulator compares sharing databases, joint meetings and shared calendars to keep different agencies in step on a case. This compares ways to:","coordinate work and organize information with other agencies",["avoid agencies","hide information","duplicate work"],"Interagency coordination.")
H("768.d.2.B",4,"Coordinating with other agencies helps by:","avoiding duplicated effort and gaps",["adding duplicates","increasing gaps","reducing communication"],"Coordination.")
H("768.d.2.C",3,"In a simulation, a spokesperson releases a clear, honest statement about an inspection finding so rumors do not spread. This simulates:","releasing public information to minimize controversy",["hiding results","spreading rumors","blaming others"],"Clear communication reduces controversy.")
H("768.d.2.C",4,"To minimize controversy when releasing news, an agency should be:","timely, accurate and clear",["slow","vague","secretive"],"Timely, accurate, clear.")
H("768.d.2.D",3,"After a research team sends its findings, the field office never hears back and cannot act. This identifies problems that arise regarding the:","flow of information after research responses",["flow of traffic","flow of rivers","flow of music"],"Information flow can break.")
H("768.d.2.D",4,"One cause of poor information flow in an organization is:","unclear reporting channels",["too many meetings only","clear instructions","good tools"],"Unclear channels.")
H("768.d.2.E",3,"A team sets up a shared dashboard and a weekly update call so field staff and analysts see the same facts. This creates a solution to the problem of:","information flow and communication",["lunch scheduling","uniform colors","parking spots"],"Fix communication gaps.")
H("768.d.2.E",4,"A simple fix for communication gaps is to:","set regular updates and a shared record",["avoid updates","use rumors","change nothing"],"Regular updates.")
H("768.d.2.F",3,"A trainee gives an official an accurate, well-sourced briefing on a rule and its likely effects. This demonstrates the ability to:","present authoritative advice to interested parties",["avoid questions","guess answers","use jokes"],"Authoritative advice is sourced.")
H("768.d.2.F",4,"Advice is authoritative when it is based on:","verified facts, rules and expertise",["hunches","rumors","popularity"],"Facts and expertise.")
H("768.d.3.A",3,"An analyst reviews inspection results and sees repeated safety lapses in one plant that need discussion with management. This analyzes data to:","identify matters needing negotiation for resolution",["ignore lapses","delay inspections","close the plant"],"Data points to what needs resolution.")
H("768.d.3.A",4,"Repeated violations in the same plant usually indicate:","a systemic problem needing resolution",["perfect compliance","a one-time accident","no need for action"],"Patterns signal systemic issues.")
H("768.d.3.B",3,"A class explores examples of firms that falsify records, skip required tests or ignore posted limits. This explores and identifies:","different noncompliant practices",["successful practices","rule-following","best practices"],"Noncompliance takes many forms.")
H("768.d.3.B",4,"Falsifying inspection records is an example of:","noncompliance",["compliance","good practice","routine work"],"Falsification is noncompliance.")
H("768.d.3.C",3,"A regulator weighs a warning letter, a fine, a compliance order or court action as fits a violation. This recommends application of:","administrative and judicial remedies",["rewards","prizes","bonuses"],"Remedies range from administrative to judicial.")
H("768.d.3.C",4,"A fine imposed by an agency without going to court is an example of an:","administrative remedy",["judicial remedy","criminal sentence","private contract"],"Agency fines are administrative.")
H("768.d.3.D",3,"A trainee writes a sample report on a case so future auditors can handle similar cases the same way. This produces:","mock reports that provide a basis for handling similar cases or audits",["private diaries","jokes","menus"],"Reports set precedent.")
H("768.d.3.D",4,"A well-written case report helps future auditors by:","providing a consistent reference",["hiding the facts","adding confusion","wasting time"],"Reports guide future work.")
H("768.d.4.A",3,"An inspector measures a part's size, watches a machine run and reviews how a product is made at each step. This conducts:","dimensional, operational and process inspections",["pop quizzes","taste tests","fashion shows"],"Types of inspection.")
H("768.d.4.A",4,"An inspection that checks the size of a manufactured part is a:","dimensional inspection",["process inspection only","menu inspection","music inspection"],"Dimensional = measurements.")
H("768.d.4.B",3,"An inspector compares measured readings with the limits in the specification and notes any outside the range. This measures:","compliance with standards, specifications and requirements",["opinions of staff","rumors","colors"],"Compare to specs.")
H("768.d.4.B",4,"A product that measures outside its specification is:","out of compliance",["in compliance","perfect","exempt"],"Out of spec.")
H("768.d.4.C",3,"A quality inspector tracks defect counts, temperatures and finish across several batches. This monitors:","a variety of quality characteristics",["lunch trends","hat sizes","game scores"],"Monitor quality.")
H("768.d.4.C",4,"Tracking defects over many batches helps to:","spot trends and fix causes",["avoid improvement","hide defects","ignore data"],"Trend tracking.")
H("768.d.4.D",3,"A student studies how a small deviation might bring a warning but a large one could shut down a facility or cause injury. This researches:","consequences of degrees of noncompliance",["menus","songs","maps"],"Consequences scale with severity.")
H("768.d.4.D",4,"Penalties for noncompliance generally increase with:","the severity of the violation",["the weather","the day of the week","office size"],"Severity matters.")
H("768.d.4.E",3,"Before deciding on a penalty, an investigator reviews past complaints and the conditions in which a violation occurred. This investigates:","the history and circumstances of violations",["last year's menu","a game score","a travel plan"],"History informs response.")
H("768.d.4.E",4,"A company with a long history of repeated violations will likely face:","stronger enforcement action",["no action","rewards","less oversight"],"Repeat offenders face tougher action.")
H("768.d.4.F",3,"When an inspector cannot judge a chemical process alone, she calls a specialist and refers the case to the proper office. This secures:","expertise and makes referrals as needed",["no help","excuses","delays"],"Know when to seek expertise.")
H("768.d.4.F",4,"An inspector should make a referral when a case:","falls outside the inspector's authority or expertise",["is easy","is routine","is closed"],"Refer beyond scope.")

